# Core relations contract

- `core-relations` is the backing database implementation. It supports both parallel and serial modes. By default, it runs in serial mode and uses only a single thread.

Concurrency primitives live in `concurrency`, identifiers live in `numeric-id`, union-find storage lives in `union-find`, and main-crate adaptation lives in `egglog-bridge`.

Repository lint and test enforcement is defined by `Makefile`, `clippy.toml`, and `.config/nextest.toml`.
CLASS: CONTRACT
